the daycare providers

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:59.010
are really being compliant and
providing a safer environment.

00:13:59.010 --> 00:14:01.560
MTX built a background
record check application

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:05.160
that can be rolled out to
these different use cases

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:07.410
and making sure that
we're managing risk.

00:14:07.410 --> 00:14:09.210
As part of the
managing risk, we need

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:10.890
to be able to
understand, what are

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:13.680
some of the regulatory
statutes that we need to make

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:15.840
sure that we are compliant?

00:14:15.840 --> 00:14:17.550
And also making sure
that we're enforcing

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:20.190
those on a regular
basis and be able to do

00:14:20.190 --> 00:14:23.160
some of the inspection visit
using cloud technology,

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:24.950
such as Google Meet.

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:28.780
And whether you schedule remote
visits or in-person visits,

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:31.720
there's certain ways you can
use this technology as you go

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:34.080
and be able to have those
informations bubble out so you

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:37.320
can have an informed
decision-making process as part

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:38.790
of your agencies.

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:43.380
Now, we do look at creating a
safer environment for children,

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:46.380
whether it is
back-to-school solutions

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:51.120
or really creating a solution
for the essential workforce,

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:54.035
whether they can put
their kids in a daycare.

00:14:54.035 --> 00:14:55.410
All of these
solutions are really

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:58.320
relevant in how you
could promote and have

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:01.860
a meaningful,
insightful informations

00:15:01.860 --> 00:15:04.770
to make informed decisions
in the way you digitize

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:06.090
and transform.

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:09.380
Now, it is common sense
to say that, well,

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:12.760
why wouldn't we create a safer
environment for children?

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:15.900
Well, it's really difficult when
you had the paper-based systems

00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:18.000
or really antiquated
systems or systems that

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.800
do not talk to each other.

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:23.490
Our comprehensive child
protective solutions really

00:15:23.490 --> 00:15:25.950
enables decision
makers to have insight

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:29.220
into the different activities
across different business units

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:33.690
and bubble up informations
is that if providers

00:15:33.690 --> 00:15:36.160
or foster parents are
really breaking the rule

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:40.080
and creating an unsafe
environment for children,

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:42.930
then some of the subsidy
programs could be frozen,

00:15:42.930 --> 00:15:45.660
and then certain
penalty could be

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:48.940
imposed to make sure that we
continue to create a safer

00:15:48.940 --> 00:15:51.780
environment for the children.

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:54.540
So let's take a look at
the next topic, which

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:57.270
is the quality of life.

00:15:57.270 --> 00:16:00.840
Whether you are decision
makers at a CIO level

00:16:00.840 --> 00:16:06.040
or deputy commissioners
or business unit leaders,

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:08.690
there's a constant conversation.

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:12.500
It's that, is it safe for
us to go back to work?

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:16.440
Or how should we really
roll out the strategy?

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:18.780
There's a meaningful
conversation to have.

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:24.650
And that is that do you need
to rush in your strategy to put

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:27.352
everyone back into workforce?

00:16:27.352 --> 00:16:29.060
What are some meaningful
insight in terms

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:34.060
of, is there benefits having
folks working remotely?

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:35.810
And if you do, what
are some of the things

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:37.370
you need to be aware of?

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:39.815
We strongly recommend using
the Google Cloud technology

00:16:39.815 --> 00:16:42.310
to create a collaborative
environment,

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:44.960
a connected community.

00:16:44.960 --> 00:16:47.720
The research has
shown that when you

00:16:47.720 --> 00:16:52.520
create a connected community
for the remote workforce using

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:55.800
the right tool and
technology for collaboration,

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:58.770
you create a happy workforce.

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:00.240
When you create a
happy workforce,

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:03.790
there is a direct correlation
to increase in productivity.

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:06.119
So we strongly
recommend that as you

00:17:06.119 --> 00:17:08.280
are dealing with this
unpredictable time,

00:17:08.280 --> 00:17:11.280
to look at the cloud
technologies such as Google

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:14.220
Cloud Platform to make
sure that we can enable

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:18.260
those collaboration tools,
including the Google Meet,

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:22.650
to make sure that your
employees feel connected.

00:17:22.650 --> 00:17:26.630
The next, you are going
to be looked to accelerate

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:29.160
the digital transformation.

00:17:29.160 --> 00:17:32.280
This year with the
COVID responses,

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.770
it kind of forced us
to really look at this

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:38.520
and really accelerate all
of our needs in that aspect.

00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:42.270
The good news is you do have
some Care Act funding that will

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:44.250
expire at the end of the year.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:45.750
Some of you have
already accelerated

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:47.770
those digital transformation.

00:17:47.770 --> 00:17:49.607
There are some of
those other technology

00:17:49.607 --> 00:17:52.190
that you may have that you can
potentially bring to the Google

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:55.140
Cloud technology
and also subsidize

00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:57.920
those with this Care
Act funding and support

00:17:57.920 --> 00:18:00.690
your remote workforce.

00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:02.550
As part of that
process, do set up

00:18:02.550 --> 00:18:05.130
some metric in
terms of whether you

00:18:05.130 --> 00:18:07.860
care about the throughput,
work-life balance,

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:11.310
or connected community
that increases

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:13.380
productivity in the workforce.

00:18:13.380 --> 00:18:16.830
Have those meaningful
metrics that are defined.

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:19.185
And also rules are built
out using our solutions

00:18:19.185 --> 00:18:22.560
within Google Cloud technology
using BigQuery and [INAUDIBLE]

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:25.170
so you can visualize at
the organization level

00:18:25.170 --> 00:18:26.910
or at the business unit level.

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:28.920
And this will ensure
that as you're

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:31.743
supporting the remote
workforce or there

00:18:31.743 --> 00:18:35.690
is an incremental slow process
to get back to normalcy,

00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:39.420
there is a way you can
support the quality of life

00:18:39.420 --> 00:18:42.600
for your remote workforce
using Google technology.

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:44.670
With that being said,
we're on the last topic.

00:18:44.670 --> 00:18:47.220
And Nick, I'll turn it over
to you for the robotic process

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:49.140
automation.

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:50.770
NICHOLAS WHITNEY:
Thank you, Das.

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:53.510
As we look at the theme
of doing more with less,

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:56.493
we have a lot of ability to
improve our worker experience

00:18:56.493 --> 00:18:58.660
at the same time that we
reduce the amount of effort

00:18:58.660 --> 00:19:01.600
that we're putting into
a standardized workforce.

00:19:01.600 --> 00:19:03.190
We really want to
be able to automate

00:19:03.190 --> 00:19:04.480
our repetitive actions.

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:06.663
We want to be able to
increase our quality,

00:19:06.663 --> 00:19:08.830
and want to be able to
reduce the human error that's

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:10.930
associated with
these manual actions.

00:19:10.930 --> 00:19:13.510
So we want to minimize
any manual tasks

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:14.980
and start to be
able to move those

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:17.260
into system-based workflows.

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.420
As we look at the bots
that are available to us

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:22.570
or that we can build, we have
a lot of areas of improvement.

00:19:22.570 --> 00:19:25.460
Finance has the ability to
streamline their AP and AR

00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:27.970
including things like vendor
onboarding, where they

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:30.250
may no longer be able to
bring people into an office

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:33.190
to be able to sign paperwork
and be able to actually handle

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:34.450
that in person.

00:19:34.450 --> 00:19:36.730
They now need to be able
to do this remotely.

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:38.230
So we can set up
the bots that allow

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:40.870
them to streamline this process
that would have historically

00:19:40.870 --> 00:19:42.330
been done on paper.

00:19:42.330 --> 00:19:43.830
As we look at the
approvals, we want

00:19:43.830 --> 00:19:45.038
to be able to automate those.

00:19:45.038 --> 00:19:46.955
Those are no longer again
going to be stamped.

00:19:46.955 --> 00:19:48.430
They're not going to be in ink.

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:50.970
We want to be able to
move those into a system.

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:53.670
And as we look at HR, especially
with some of the challenges

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:55.878
that come out from COVID of
perhaps [? standing up ?]

00:19:55.878 --> 00:19:58.680
call centers for responding
to issues that they may not

00:19:58.680 --> 00:20:00.540
historically have
handled, we want

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:02.640
to be able to automate
the onboarding,

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:05.580
orchestrate the systems that
need to be put together.

00:20:05.580 --> 00:20:08.190
As we look at doing that
automation of the onboarding,

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:10.080
we can increase
our responsiveness

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:12.300
and improve our
worker experience

00:20:12.300 --> 00:20:14.700
by using bots to be
responsive to what

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:16.490
comes back from those people.

00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:18.270
If we have forms that
need to be set out,

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:20.410
if we have signatures
that are required,

00:20:20.410 --> 00:20:22.140
we can ensure that
those processes are

00:20:22.140 --> 00:20:24.937
streamlined, efficient,
and providing a good worker

00:20:24.937 --> 00:20:27.270
experience to people who may
not have as much experience

00:20:27.270 --> 00:20:29.383
with those forms.

00:20:29.383 --> 00:20:30.800
As we look at these
tools, there's

00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:34.850
also a great example here of
being able to use the AI tool.

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:36.530
One of the AI tools
that we suggested

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:40.960
is a Maverick AI tool, which is
our internal Maverick platform.

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:43.130
This has been built on
a Google Cloud platform

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:47.030
and allows us to reduce the
amount of effort that is spent

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:49.880
on tasks that are lower value.

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:53.170
Those tasks can instead
be done by the platform

00:20:53.170 --> 00:20:55.640
and allow us to do something
like scanning documents

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:58.340
to ensure that they are
accurately filled out

00:20:58.340 --> 00:20:59.990
and sending them back
out to the people

00:20:59.990 --> 00:21:01.580
if they're not completed.

00:21:01.580 --> 00:21:04.790
And whatever rules-based
platform action is,

00:21:04.790 --> 00:21:06.680
we need to be able to follow up.

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:10.190
This allows us to focus our
people's time and energy

00:21:10.190 --> 00:21:11.930
where there's higher value.

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:15.105
And instead of having them
scan 100% of the documents,

00:21:15.105 --> 00:21:16.480
they may only need
to be involved

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:17.860
with 20% of the documents.

00:21:17.860 --> 00:21:20.976
They can review those and
be far more efficient.

00:21:20.976 --> 00:21:22.930
Das, is there anything
you want to add?

