00:22:01.570 --> 00:22:04.810
in the RPA [INAUDIBLE]
with Maverick AI platform,

00:22:04.810 --> 00:22:07.520
how can you really solve
some of the challenges?

00:22:07.520 --> 00:22:10.580
Nick, let's talk about--

00:22:10.580 --> 00:22:12.910
there's a lot of folks who
will talk about, well, AI

00:22:12.910 --> 00:22:14.920
is buzz words.

00:22:14.920 --> 00:22:17.830
We are seeing some
real-world examples

00:22:17.830 --> 00:22:19.430
and we're solving
real-world problems

00:22:19.430 --> 00:22:22.690
for government agencies
and the private sector.

00:22:22.690 --> 00:22:29.900
If I'm a CIO, what can I look
toward in terms of preparations

00:22:29.900 --> 00:22:31.960
in solving some of my
challenges using AI?

00:22:31.960 --> 00:22:33.485
How do I start?

00:22:33.485 --> 00:22:35.110
NICHOLAS WHITNEY: So
what we like to do

00:22:35.110 --> 00:22:38.050
is we like to start with a
journey map of if we were

00:22:38.050 --> 00:22:41.560
able to look into the future and
say, what does a perfect state

00:22:41.560 --> 00:22:42.670
look like?

00:22:42.670 --> 00:22:44.410
We want to understand
that vision

00:22:44.410 --> 00:22:46.335
and understanding
that business goal.

00:22:46.335 --> 00:22:47.710
What that allows us to do, then.

00:22:47.710 --> 00:22:50.380
Is kind of look at what is
maybe a low-hanging fruit.

00:22:50.380 --> 00:22:51.963
Sometimes things
look like they're

00:22:51.963 --> 00:22:53.380
going to be more
complex, but it's

00:22:53.380 --> 00:22:55.780
something you could
actually do in a far more

00:22:55.780 --> 00:22:56.710
efficient fashion.

00:22:56.710 --> 00:22:58.725
Allows you to pilot
the functionality,

00:22:58.725 --> 00:23:00.350
ensure that you're
comfortable with it,

00:23:00.350 --> 00:23:02.290
start to build
that all over time.

00:23:02.290 --> 00:23:04.060
It doesn't necessarily
need to be that we

00:23:04.060 --> 00:23:05.410
boil the ocean on day one.

00:23:05.410 --> 00:23:07.483
We can solve a single
business problem,

00:23:07.483 --> 00:23:09.150
free up some resources,
and then move on

00:23:09.150 --> 00:23:11.320
to the next business problem.

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:13.540
Ultimately, that
kind of evaluation

00:23:13.540 --> 00:23:15.850
of the security,
evaluation of the workflow,

00:23:15.850 --> 00:23:18.947
and starting out in a measured
and controlled fashion

00:23:18.947 --> 00:23:20.905
is something that we've
seen be very successful

00:23:20.905 --> 00:23:23.620
and start to really
free up those resources

00:23:23.620 --> 00:23:25.180
to move on to the
next area where

00:23:25.180 --> 00:23:29.823
there is better focus and better
area of improvement for us.

00:23:29.823 --> 00:23:30.990
DAS NOBEL: Yeah, absolutely.

00:23:30.990 --> 00:23:31.698
And thanks, Nick.

